# ============================================================================
# Triage 2026-09-14 — the curl 8.21.0 + openssl 3.6.3 advisory batches
# (#1614 main / #1615 dev). A feed event, not a closure change: the 2026-09-11
# nightly (run 34583730623) was green on the SAME pin (c25784012c) that the
# 2026-09-12 run (34684718095) went red on, and the findings delta is 16 new
# blocking CVEs across exactly two packages, nothing removed, no expiry fired.
# Both advisory sets were published by the projects on their fix-release day
# (openssl advisories dated 2026-08-25, shipped with 3.6.4; curl's with
# 8.22.0) and reached the NVD feed in the 09-11 -> 09-12 window.
#
# Every entry is a real product+version match verified ONLINE against the
# upstream security pages (curl.se vuln-8.21.0, openssl-library.org
# vulnerabilities index): all nine curl CVEs affect <= 8.21.0 and are fixed in
# 8.22.0; all seven blocking openssl CVEs affect 3.6.0 before 3.6.4. (A 17th
# finding, openssl CVE-2026-63074 at 5.9, is below the gate's 7.0 threshold
# and needs no entry.) NVD-vs-upstream severity is wildly apart on this batch:
# NVD scores 7.4–9.8 where curl rates eight of nine Low (one Medium) and
# openssl rates all seven Low/Moderate.
#
# Provenance: curl is a direct member of the image env (flake.nix), built the
# nixpkgs default way — OpenSSL backend, ldapSupport=false, no wolfSSL,
# HTTP/3 on. openssl is in-closure via curl/openssh/python/nix and appears as
# two same-version store paths (bootstrap + final stage), which is why the
# gate prints the seven openssl CVEs twice.
#
# Remediation lever: exists, but has nowhere to land today — the exact rsync
# situation this slot previously held. curl 8.22.0 (nixpkgs #561666) and
# openssl 3.6.4 (nixpkgs #557618) are both merged to staging-26.05 and are
# riding the OPEN staging-next-26.05 iteration-7 PR (nixpkgs #563094) toward
# release-26.05; neither is in release-26.05 or the pinned nixos-26.05 yet,
# so advancing the pin changes nothing. One branch hop + one weekly
# update-nixpkgs.yml advance (Mondays) should clear the whole block; expiring
# 2026-09-23 puts the review the Wednesday after the 2026-09-21 advance, so
# this block should die on remediation rather than be renewed.
# ============================================================================

Expiration: 2026-09-23
# --- curl 8.21.0 (fixed in 8.22.0). All nine are CLIENT-side: each needs the
#     user to point curl at a hostile or compromised server from an
#     interactive dev container. curl's own severity in parens after NVD's.
# CVE-2026-19931 (9.8, curl: Medium) — Negotiate ambient-user connection
#   reuse. Needs SPNEGO/Kerberos auth in use; no Kerberos deployment here.
CVE-2026-19931
# CVE-2026-18924 (9.1, curl: Low) — HTTP/2 server-push use-after-free. Server
#   push needs CURLMOPT_PUSHFUNCTION, which the curl CLI never enables.
CVE-2026-18924
# CVE-2026-82209 (8.2, curl: Low) — PSL domain-scoped cookie accepted from a
#   hostile server. Cookie engine only active with -b/-c.
CVE-2026-82209
# CVE-2026-80229 (7.5, curl: Low) — OpenSSL provider use-after-free in the
#   TLS backend teardown path.
CVE-2026-80229
# CVE-2026-80230 (7.5, curl: Low) — OpenSSL --pinnedpubkey pinning bypass.
#   Needs pinning in use; defense-in-depth downgrade, not a break-in.
CVE-2026-80230
# CVE-2026-80231 (7.5, curl: Low) — native CA store connection reuse. Needs
#   CURLSSLOPT_NATIVE_CA, not the default on Linux (cacert bundle is used).
CVE-2026-80231
# CVE-2026-80255 (7.5, curl: Low) — Secure-cookie attribute bypass via an
#   embedded tab; cookie engine, as CVE-2026-82209.
CVE-2026-80255
# CVE-2026-82208 (7.5, curl: Low) — wolfSSL CA-cache hit overrides the verify
#   callback. NOT COMPILED IN: nixpkgs curl is built against OpenSSL only.
CVE-2026-82208
# CVE-2026-13608 (7.4, curl: Low) — OpenLDAP SASL authentication bypass.
#   NOT COMPILED IN: nixpkgs builds curl with ldapSupport = false.
CVE-2026-13608
# --- openssl 3.6.3 (fixed in 3.6.4). Upstream severity in parens after
#     NVD's. The image runs no TLS/DTLS/QUIC servers and no CMP/CMS
#     processing of untrusted messages.
# CVE-2026-63073 (9.8, upstream: Low) — untrusted sender DN used as a format
#   string in CMP response validation. Needs a CMP client run against a
#   hostile CA; nothing in the image speaks CMP.
CVE-2026-63073
# CVE-2026-75803 (9.1, upstream: Low) — AEAD forgery with empty ciphertext,
#   only via direct EVP_Cipher() misuse; not the EVP_Encrypt/DecryptUpdate
#   path normal callers (curl, openssh, python) use.
CVE-2026-75803
# CVE-2026-14457 (7.5, upstream: Low) — RPK SERVER-side signature-algorithm
#   selection dereferences a missing certificate; no TLS servers here.
CVE-2026-14457
# CVE-2026-54874 (7.5, upstream: Low) — memory exhaustion buffering DTLS
#   records for a future epoch; no DTLS use in the image.
CVE-2026-54874
# CVE-2026-63072 (7.5, upstream: Moderate) — heap buffer overflow in CMS key
#   unwrapping; needs processing of attacker-supplied CMS messages.
CVE-2026-63072
# CVE-2026-63075 (7.5, upstream: Low) — QUIC ACK-only packet retention memory
#   exhaustion. Client-side HTTP/3 is compiled into curl but availability-only
#   and needs a hostile QUIC peer.
CVE-2026-63075
# CVE-2026-63076 (7.5, upstream: Moderate) — invalid pointer dereference in a
#   CMP SERVER via crafted protectionAlg; nothing runs a CMP server.
CVE-2026-63076

# ============================================================================
# Triage 2026-09-16 — the libxml2 2.15.3 advisory batch (#1636 dev /
# #1637 main). A feed event, not a closure change, and the clearest one yet:
# the 2026-09-15 nightly (run 34954313210) was green on the same pin that the
# 2026-09-16 run (35080687787) went red on, and the delta is 8 added /
# 0 removed against exactly ONE package, with no expiry fired. The whole
# CVE-2026-8613x/-8614x batch was published together on 2026-09-05 and
# reached the NVD feed in the 09-15 -> 09-16 window.
#
# Only ONE of the eight clears the gate's 7.0 threshold and needs an entry.
# The other seven — CVE-2026-86137 (2.9), -86138 (6.9), -86139 (6.9),
# -86141 (2.9), -86142 (6.9), -86143 (6.9), -86144 (5.6) — are deliberately
# absent from this register, as the glibc block records for its own
# sub-threshold pair.
#
# Provenance: libxml2 is not a direct member of the image env; it is pulled in
# transitively (verified with `nix why-depends`). The pinned nixos-26.05 ships
# libxml2 2.15.3 carrying only CVE-2026-11979.patch — none of this batch is
# patched in place, so vulnix is not over-reporting here (cf. the NOTE at the
# top of this file): the finding is a true version match.
#
# Remediation lever: exists, and is the SAME one the curl + openssl block
# below is waiting on. libxml2 2.15.4 is in staging-26.05 and
# staging-next-26.05 but not in release-26.05 or the pinned nixos-26.05, so
# advancing the pin today changes nothing. curl 8.22.0, openssl 3.6.4 and
# libxml2 2.15.4 all ride the SAME open staging-next-26.05 iteration-7 PR
# (NixOS/nixpkgs#563094): one branch hop plus one weekly update-nixpkgs.yml
# advance should clear all three blocks at once, and all three should then be
# DELETED here rather than renewed.
# ============================================================================

Expiration: 2026-10-28
# --- libxml2 2.15.3 (fixed in 2.15.4). NVD scores this 8.0
#     (CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:L, cve@mitre.org); NIST's own
#     analyst scores the same defect 7.8 with PR:L. Both are LOCAL-vector: no
#     remote attack surface, which is the mitigating context for an otherwise
#     high score.
# CVE-2026-86140 (8.0) — stack-based buffer overflow via strcat in
#   xmlSnprintfElements (valid.c). The affected function only runs while
#   FORMATTING A VALIDITY ERROR MESSAGE for a DTD-validated document, so it
#   needs both DTD validation enabled and an attacker-controlled document that
#   fails validation. Nothing in this image validates untrusted XML against a
#   DTD; libxml2 is here as a transitive dependency, not as a service.
CVE-2026-86140
